<title>USA: U.S. turkey exports up 32 pct in 1996 - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. turkey exports up 32 pct in 1996 - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. turkey exports rose 32 percent to 429 million pounds in fiscal year 1996 from the previous year, and are forecast to climb to 507 million pounds in fiscal 1997, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>The department said exports are expected to boost U.S. producers' revenue by more than $150 million in fiscal 1996.</p>
<p>USDA said expanding sales to Mexico, Russia, other countries of the former Soviet Union and Poland accounted for much of the growth. In fiscal 1996, these countries bought 61 percent of total U.S. shipments, USDA said.</p>
</text>
